# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# This file is not an optimisation. Without it the context for `docker compose
# -f docker/compose.dev.yml build` is the whole repository including `.venv`
# (a few hundred MB), `apps/web/node_modules` (thousands of files), the Next.js
# build output, and whatever local SQLite state the developer has accumulated.
# The daemon target only ever needs `packages/`, `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`,
# `README.md` and `LICENSE`, and the web target needs `apps/web/` minus its
# build output.
#
# Two exclusions are correctness rather than size, and are marked as such below.
# Patterns are root-anchored with a leading `/` unless the bare name is meant to
# match at any depth — a bare `fixtures` would also drop the adapter test
# fixtures, which is not what was intended even though it happens to be
# harmless here.

# --- version control -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- local Python environment ---------------------------------------------
# Correctness: `.venv` is a Windows or macOS virtualenv on the developer's
# machine. Copying it into a Linux image would put a directory of binaries for
# the wrong platform on `PATH` ahead of the one the image just built.
/.venv
/venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
/htmlcov
/build
/dist

# --- Node ------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
/apps/web/.next
/apps/web/out
/apps/web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
/apps/web/npm-install.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- local runtime state ---------------------------------------------------
# Correctness: `.openburrow/` holds this developer's SQLite database, worktrees,
# reel exports and daemon socket. Baking it into an image would ship one
# person's sessions — including the bus log and any credential-adjacent
# metadata in it — to everyone who pulls that image.
/.openburrow
**/.openburrow
*.db
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# --- docs and scratch ------------------------------------------------------
# `mkdocs.yml` and `docs/` are published separately; the image does not serve
# them. The loose files are local run output that must not reach a layer.
/docs
/mkdocs.yml
/examples
/pytest_*.txt
/smoke_output.txt
/_f.txt
/_u.md
/_u.txt
/_u2.md
/_u3.md
